Z||000000||camon||11-10-2001||10:33 PM||||I was on the highway today going faster then I should have been (what do you expect it's a fiero). Anyway I was going about 100 or so and noticed the tach was acting really weird.<BR>It was dropping and rising at a real fast pace. I backed off the throttle and noticed it returned to normal after I backed off (doing like 70-80). Well again I picked up the throttle to about 100mph and again it was flucuating. It flucuates anywhere from 0-4k. I only noticed this starting to happen (not saying it didn't do it before because I normally drive sensably and this is one of the first time I took it up into the 100's). Well it seems to perform very good but the tach flucuates. Any idea on the cause??????<P><BR>Thanks???<P>(87 Fiero GT Auto)<P>------------------<BR>Keith||||reg||5
Z||000001||sjp777||11-10-2001||10:55 PM||||replace tach filter<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg">     <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
