Z||000003||camon||11-11-2001||03:02 AM||||Thanks!<P>Two things......<BR>Where is it located on the engine????<BR>and<BR>Where do I find one????<P>(I checked the hayes manual and they make no mention of it that I seen and I checked Auto Zone and Advance Auto's web sites and can't locate one...Do they go by a different name????)<P>Thanks again!<P>------------------<BR>Keith||||reg||1
Z||000004||WampusCat||11-11-2001||07:40 AM||||I've heard that no one makes a stock tach filter anymore.  Rodney Dickman sells one that will work but not look like the stock one.  It's the silver capacitor-looking thing next to the coil.  I put a filter from Rodney on mine and it's still erratic so I suspect I have a wiring or ground problem or maybe the chip in the tach, but most people have had good results with Rodney's filter.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jake_Dragon||11-11-2001||10:22 AM||||When I bought my GT the ignition wires were older than dirt and leaking, the Tach was all over the place.<BR>Changed the cap, rotor and wires, it runs just fine.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/left.gif">                      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif">                     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/right.gif">          <BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gt2_3.GIF"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||camon||11-12-2001||01:39 AM||||ohhh....so that's what that little chrome colored capitor is for!!!!<P>Well I will replace it some time in the future (i'll check some junk yards). If I can't locate one in that way i'll look at getting one from Rodney!<P>Thanks alot guys!<P>edited in:<BR>Ohh yeah..... I have a new accel coil ,8mm plug wires, cap and rotor so this stuff is all new (it must be the tach filter)!<P>------------------<BR>Keith<p>[This message has been edited by camon (edited 11-12-2001).]||||reg||7
